room salt_camp "Gullet Key — the Salt Camp"
  bg bg_saltcamp_wide
  width 2560
  music music_fog
  perspective horizon 312 ref 875 height 380
  walk (60,878) (120,760) (1100,740) (1500,690) (1940,700) (1950,815) (2470,815) (2500,878)
  entry 1500,800
  arrive weather_works 1500,800
  arrive reef_wreck 260,820

  sprite npc_tamhobb_body at 520,790 size 1.05 idle speaker tamhobb for tamhobb grade "saturate(0.88) brightness(0.95)"
  sprite npc_pike_body at 1700,760 size 0.95 flip idle speaker pike for pike grade "saturate(0.45) brightness(0.95)"
  sprite npc_ansel_body at 1150,780 size 1 idle speaker ansel for ansel grade "saturate(0.88) brightness(0.95)"
  sprite npc_quill_body at 1880,810 size 0.98 flip idle speaker quill for quill grade "saturate(0.88) brightness(0.95)"

  scene if not cell_scene
    set cell_scene
    talk pike at landed

  hotspot pans "the salt pans"
    area 0,480 1150x260
    nowalk
    look "Salt pans, raked white in the sun. A hundred and thirty sailors have spent three years turning the sea into something you can sell. Cray sells it."
    pickup "I lick a finger and taste. Salt. Three years of it."

  hotspot tents "the tents"
    area 690,350 1290x270
    nowalk
    look "Patched tents in rows, neat as a ledger. Somebody has sewn a name over every doorway, so nobody forgets whose is whose. Or who they are."

  hotspot washing "the washing"
    area 1000,430 680x140
    nowalk
    look "Shirts on a line. Every few days one goes missing and turns up later as part of a flag. Nobody complains. I gather it's an honour."

  hotspot flats "the reef flats"
    area 0,300 560x180
    stand 260,820
    look "The reef flats, running out to the lagoon in a mile of coral and sudden deep pockets. Somebody who'd crossed them a hundred times might know the way."
    open "Not without somebody who knows where the holes are. The holes are very patient."
    walk "Not without somebody who knows where the holes are. The holes are very patient."
    # Crossable once Quill is out: you came over them, and Ansel is a bonus, not a gate.
    state if quill_free
      exit reef_wreck
      look "The reef flats, staked across to the wreck at low tide. My father's road. He goes wrong at the third stake."
      open "We cross the flats, stake by stake. At the third one I don't follow my father."

  hotspot hut "the store hut"
    area 1990,280 570x520
    stand 2100,840
    look "A stout store hut with a barred window and a padlock the size of a ham. Inside, pending inspection, a navigator, looking out at me through the bars."
    open "Padlocked. Pike has the key on a string round his neck, next to his whistle."
    talk "I go to the bars."
      talk quill3 at hut
    pull "The padlock is not open to argument. Pike, on the other hand, is open to paperwork."
    state if quill_free
      look "The store hut, open now, empty but for salt fish and a tremendous sense of anticlimax."
      talk "Nobody in there now but the fish."
        nothing

  hotspot tamhobb "Tam Hobb"
    area 440,470 170x320
    stand 700,800
    look "A big man raking salt, with a shaved head and a black beard and a face I've already seen, older and sadder, at the Marrow's mess table."
    talk "He leans on his rake and looks at me as if I'm a knot somebody tied badly."
      talk tamhobb
    give "“Nothing in here's mine to keep, clerk. Hang on to it.”"

  hotspot pike "Pike"
    area 1620,480 160x280
    stand 1560,790
    look "Pike, on camp duty, clutching his clipboard and avoiding Quill's eye through the bars. He looks like a man who has done his job and hates it."
    talk "He snaps to attention, slightly less snappily than before."
      talk pike at camp
    give "“Only forms, sir. Sorry, sir.”"
    state if quill_free
      talk: talk pike at done

  hotspot ansel "Ansel Fenn"
    show if quill_free
    area 1060,450 190x330
    stand 1300,790
    look "My father. Sunburnt to the colour of a ship's biscuit, beard like a burst mattress, a needle in his lapel and an L on his cuff. He looks exactly the same and nothing like."
    talk "He's grinning. He hasn't stopped since he dropped the flag."
      talk ansel
    give "“For me? Is it a flag? It's not a flag. Pity.”"
    state if ansel_met
      talk: talk ansel at hub

  hotspot quill "Quill"
    show if quill_free
    area 1800,520 170x290
    stand 1740,800
    look "Quill, free, with salt in her hair and a look on her face I'd like to file somewhere safe."
    talk "She turns round before I get there. She's stopped pretending she doesn't."
      talk quill3 at camp
    give "“Keep it. You've already given me the best thing on this island, and it was a form.”"
    state if has flag16
      talk: talk quill3 at flag

  use stamp on bill if knows_form9 and not form9
    "I turn the Bill of Health over and write on the back, in my best customs hand: FORM 9. RELEASE OF DETAINED PERSONS UPON INSPECTION. Then I stamp it, which makes it true."
    set form9
    sound chime
  use stamp on bill if form9
    "Both sides stamped. Any more and it'll be mostly stamp."
  use bill on pike if form9 and not quill_free
    "I hand Pike the Bill of Health, back side up."
    take bill
    set quill_free
    sound chime
    talk pike at form9
  use bill on pike if knows_form9 and not quill_free
    "“That's your Bill of Health, sir. It's lovely. It isn't a Form 9.” He looks at its blank back, and then at me, hopefully."
  use bill on pike
    "“You're inspected, sir. You're fine. It's the lady who's pending.”"
  use bill on hut
    "The padlock can't read. Pike can."
  use crowbar on hut
    "I measure the crowbar against the padlock. Then I look at Pike's whistle, and at the forty Weather men it would fetch. A form, then."
  use flag16 on ansel
    "“Not to me, son. Up the mast. That's what they're for.”"
  use compass on ansel
    "He laughs out loud. “Still pointing at the Old Nail. Some of us are very loyal.”"
  use ansel_log on ansel
    "He reads the last page and hands it back rather quickly. “You weren't meant to read that one. …I'm glad you did. Keep it.”"
  use stamp on pike
    "He holds out his hand to be stamped, hopefully. I'm tempted. I'm a professional."
  use ansel_log on tamhobb
    "He finds his own name in it and taps it twice. “Still here, Captain,” he says to the page."
  combos quill_combos
  use stamp on hut
    "I stamp the padlock. It now looks officially locked, which is worse."
  use ansel_log on pike
    "He won't take it. “Captain's private papers, sir. I'd need a form to read them, and I'd need a stronger stomach to want to.”"
